I was trying to answer a ggplot question on Stack Overflow <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/24769934/ggplot-bar-chart-with-two-dataframes?noredirect=1> and came up with a result I couldn't explain. I'm hoping someone here will have the answer.

The questioner wanted to plot the following two data frames separately, but without having the bars overlap:

x <- data.frame(dat=rep(seq(1,4),3),let=rep("X"))
y <- data.frame(dat=rep(seq(1,4),4),let=rep("y"))

He tried the following, but the bars are right on top of each other:

