Dear  google group

I’m new to R and struggle with the code of a multi-plot panel. I need to arrange 45 bar charts on one page with annotations at top, bottom and left hand side. I used ggplot2 to create the plots and grid to place the plots on the single page. I’m happy with the location of the plots and the annotations. I’m really unhappy with the margins between the plots. The margins between the plots are too big and the plots as such a far too small. I guess the source of the problem is in the grid.layout  function. Changing the ggplot2 margins (via theme) did not show any changes.

I would be very happy when someone could help me how I could increase plot size and decrease margins between plots grid.layout cells respectively. Below, you’ll find a simplified version of the code I’ve used.

Many thanks for your help!

Ulrika

library(ggplot2)
library(grid)
